zoompilot/jetlink d26001b4161f33bab28d806de6a99b96325a429b (v0.8.7).
Source and exclusions: ../upstream-sync.json.
StarPilot changes: 40 held frames per 10 s; USB receive steering on core 3.
Valid non-graph warp captures retain full replay when graph-only optimization is unavailable;
a paired capture replays its two transform copies on buffers resolved once and its kernels linked once
(warp._PairedReplay), after warping random frames byte-for-byte as the full replay does.
The StarPilot adapter, process lifecycle and diagnostics live in ../openpilot/starpilot/.
A host configured at high-speed after a late device-side start is reconnected once for super-speed.
The warp reads its buffers through tinygrad's own host mapping where this tinygrad lacks as_memoryview(force_zero_copy).

StarPilot runtime 0.8.7+starpilot.1 (not an upstream release): persistent cable
listener with negotiated SCM_RIGHTS handoff of idle app connections, legacy
borrower fallback, explicit provisioning lease cleanup, bounded connection
retries, deterministic failed-socket cleanup, and additive connection guidance.
The host wire protocol remains 3.
The standalone StarPilot warp format, build entry point and validated paired
replay are retained instead of upstream's driving_warp dictionary format.
Fallback reset supports both native packed state and StarPilot catalog queues.
The adapter implements API 3 using control state supplied by modeld each frame.
StarPilot opts into following the host's loaded model when there is no manual
big-model pick. Protocol 3's existing ENGINE_REQ returns the loaded engine's
spec with nbytes=0; no host changes, catalog lookup, or upload are needed.
App observations are tagged in the spec record, separate from manual picks.
